2. Presentation templates (collegebeamer.sty and derivatives)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The files templates/*/collegebeamer.sty under the packs:

    academic, emerald, graphite, navy

(and their visual/theme derivatives in the same directories) are based on:

    college-beamer
    Author : Qilong Liu
    Source : https://github.com/liu-qilong/college-beamer
    License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

That project is itself derived from:

    SINTEF Presentation
    Author : Federico Zenith
    License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

These four packs share that common ancestor. They are separate design treatments
(palette, typography, chrome), not four independent theme designs.

TeXDeck's modifications to the college-beamer style (non-exhaustive) include:

  - Stripped multi-institution package options down to a single retained theme path
  - Changed theme colors: each pack uses its own maincolorRGB / layout tweaks
  - Unified CJK fonts to the Fandol family (typically FandolKai / FandolFang as
    available in TeX Live; no system-specific Chinese fonts required)
  - Rewrote QA / thank-you page copy
  - Layout and typography variants per pack (e.g. academic: Palatino + newtxmath;
    graphite: report-style itemize / footer rule / greyscale treatment)
  - Replaced third-party trademark logo/background assets with neutral
    placeholders under src/brand/ and retargeted image paths accordingly

Per CC BY 4.0, you must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the license,
and indicate if changes were made when you redistribute these style files.


